          <th>Focus</th>
          <th>Skill to build</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Role family"><strong>Process analyst</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Focus">Map and measure current processes</td>
          <td data-label="Skill to build">Mapping and spreadsheets</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Role family"><strong>Process improvement</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Focus">Redesign for speed and quality</td>
          <td data-label="Skill to build">Problem solving and statistics basics</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Role family"><strong>Automation and workflow</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Focus">Move steps to tools</td>
          <td data-label="Skill to build">Workflow tools and logic</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Role family"><strong>Quality and compliance</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Focus">Keep processes within rules</td>
          <td data-label="Skill to build">Documentation and attention to detail</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Role family"><strong>Transformation roles</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Focus">Lead change across teams</td>
          <td data-label="Skill to build">Communication and change handling</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Pick one family and read ten notices for it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="improve">A simple improvement cycle you can practise</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Step</th>
          <th>What to do</th>
          <th>Output</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Step"><strong>Map</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to do">Draw the current steps</td>
          <td data-label="Output">A one-page flow</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Step"><strong>Measure</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to do">Time each step and count errors</td>
          <td data-label="Output">A small table</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Step"><strong>Find</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to do">Pick the biggest delay or error source</td>
          <td data-label="Output">One target</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Step"><strong>Fix</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to do">Try one change for two weeks</td>
          <td data-label="Output">A trial</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Step"><strong>Check</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What to do">Measure again and record</td>
          <td data-label="Output">A before and after note</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="tools">Tools to try, from simplest to most advanced</h2>

  <p>
    Start with the simplest tool that does the job. Tool names change, so focus on the idea.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Level</th>
          <th>What it is</th>
          <th>What to practise</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Level"><strong>Paper and pen</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it is">A hand-drawn flow with arrows</td>
          <td data-label="What to practise">Mapping steps and handoffs</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Level"><strong>Spreadsheet</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it is">A table of steps, times and errors</td>
          <td data-label="What to practise">Counting and simple charts</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Level"><strong>Free diagram tools</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it is">Drawn flow charts that can be shared</td>
          <td data-label="What to practise">Clean maps others can read</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Level"><strong>Free workflow or form tools</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it is">Simple automations between forms and sheets</td>
          <td data-label="What to practise">One automated step</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Level"><strong>Scripting basics</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What it is">Short scripts for repeated tasks</td>
          <td data-label="What to practise">Only after the process is stable</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Employers care less about which tool you used than whether the process got better.
  </p>

  <h2 id="change">Why process changes fail, and how to prevent it</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Failure</th>
          <th>Cause</th>
          <th>Prevention</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Failure"><strong>Staff ignore the new way</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Cause">They were not asked</td>
          <td data-label="Prevention">Involve two users in the design</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Failure"><strong>It works only on paper</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Cause">The map missed real exceptions</td>
          <td data-label="Prevention">Walk the process on the floor</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Failure"><strong>Savings do not appear</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Cause">Nobody measured before</td>
          <td data-label="Prevention">Record the baseline first</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Failure"><strong>It breaks after a month</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Cause">No owner</td>
          <td data-label="Prevention">Name one person to keep it running</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="money">Money: course fees and the 10 percent test</h2>

  <p>
    As a rule of thumb and not a research finding, keep a degree or course fee near a tenth of the family's total education budget, and treat spending above roughly a fifth as a serious caution that needs course-specific evidence.
  </p>
  <p>
    An illustration, not a real fee: on a Rs 8 lakh education budget, a tenth is Rs 80,000 for the main course, and a fifth is Rs 1.6 lakh as a serious caution. The rest can fund a laptop, practice time and a reserve.
  </p>
  <p>
    Test the field with free courses and one finished project before paying for a long programme. Do not borrow heavily for a course whose graduates cannot show placement in a specific role.
  </p>

